    {
      "block_id": "2605.00155_p20_b21",
      "text": "In experiments, the KL term is estimated on sampled completions with the well-known\nk3 estimator of Schulman [2020]: for z(k) = log \u03c00(y(k) | x) \u2212log \u00af\u03c0(y(k) | x), average\nexp(z(k)) \u2212z(k) \u22121 over the group. This statistic is nonnegative samplewise, has lower\n",
      "bbox": [
        72.0,
        416.62,
        523.54,
        464.36
      ],
      "rendered_bbox": [
        288,
        1666,
